  "body": "**Blocked by:** #157\n\n## Context\n\nJSON resources are complete. Files are the sole binary exception and must retain the same authenticated, deterministic discipline.\n\n## Task\n\nImplement `POST /api/files` as a raw streamed body with `Content-Type` and `X-Filename`. Enforce `maxFileSizeMb` first from `Content-Length` when present and always through a streaming byte counter; abort and clean partial state on overflow. Compute SHA-256 while streaming, deduplicate through the unique `content_hash`, and create blob metadata plus the Files database row transactionally. If existing rows already reference the blob, return the lowest-ID row deterministically. Implement authenticated `GET /api/blobs/:id` with byte ranges, `ETag=content_hash`, conditional responses, safe filename handling, and `Content-Disposition`; honor `?disposition=inline` only for a fixed safe MIME allowlist and always set `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Streaming upload/download, limits, hashing/dedup, transactional metadata, Range/ETag and response hardening.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Presigned URLs, resumable uploads, total-storage quota, and unauthenticated blob access.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Unknown/chunked length cannot bypass the hard byte limit and failed uploads leave no partial blob or row.\n- Concurrent identical uploads converge on one content hash and deterministic Files row.\n- Range/ETag/download-name/inline-allowlist tests cover valid, invalid, and malicious inputs.\n",
